      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi, why do we need to link the Trusty VM\u0027s deferring rollback protection check to DT?\n\nThe DT field `defer-rollback-protection` is currently a SecretKeeper-specific configuration. Trusty VM\u0027s rollback protection should remain separate, as they are independent features.\n\nIn http://b/395794671#comment5, I meant the presence of the `deferred_rollback` capability alone in the kernel\u0027s vbmeta should trigger pvmfw to skip rollback protection. SecretKeeper\u0027s existing checks in pvmfw, like DT field validation, should not interfere with the Trusty VM flow.\n\nCC @armellel@google.com",
